  "sourceBoundContracts": [
    "SwEditWin delegates represented Border/Margin tracking to persistent SwView horizontal/vertical Ruler owners with source5px tolerance; original Writer carrier and document hit remain apply owners.",
    "SVTOOLS owns captured physical axis and native start/move/end/cancel hook state; SVX owns independent SvxColumnItem copies, modifier flags, constraints, transient geometry and source uint16 percent/width-block buffers, without SW/browser reverse imports.",
    "Represented column linear/proportional and row ordinary/proportional/current-line policies retain captured values and original model/history; class declines unrepresented writing/frame-column contexts.",
    "Writer ExecuteTabWin-shaped value conversion preserves original SwTabCols entry owners/constraints and native visibility. Row current-line flags reach original core; column apply preserves the prior ordinary shared-column contract because SwDoc/SwTable explicitly reject independent row geometry.",
    "Native Library_svx uses svt/vcl and Library_sw uses svt; graph permits only required native directions, preserving reverse/browser ownership gates."
  ],
  "residuals": [
    "Independent per-row column widths/current-line column apply remain unsupported in SwDoc and SwTable. This is a real upstream gap requiring the next core correction, not a registered intentional exception.",
    "Full SFX bindings/listener/slot state, native VCL ruler painting/ticks/snapping/protection/page/paragraph/frame/object/tab/indent state and vertical/RTL document dragging remain partial.",
    "Represented border values retain injected logical/device conversion; complete native VCL pixel-vector ownership and window/null offsets remain incomplete.",
    "Column-margin modifier geometry and single-row paragraph-indent bottom range retain existing partial contracts; native item pooling/UNO members from prior work remain incomplete.",
    "Registered IO/open/save/recovery/settings remain byte-identical; no full upstream/module parity promotion."
  ]
}
